// Title: Potential Persistence Via Scrobj.dll COM Hijacking
// Sigma ID: fe20dda1-6f37-4379-bbe0-a98d400cae90
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-08-20 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, T1546.015
// Description: Detect use of scrobj.dll as this DLL looks for the ScriptletURL key to get the location of the
//   script to execute
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of the dll.
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/40b77d63808dd4f4eafb83949805636735a1fd15/atomics/T1546.015/T1546.015.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_persistence_scrobj_dll.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "InprocServer32\\(Default)" and RegistryValueData =~ "C:\\WINDOWS\\system32\\scrobj.dll"
